<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Elementwise Extreme Dominance). ‣ High-Dimensional Extreme-Value Amplification. ‣ 4 Mean Bias as the Dominant Source of Activation Outliers ‣ The Curse and Blessing of Mean Bias in FP4-Quantized LLM Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{ij}=\mu_{j}+Z_{ij}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{ij}=\mu_{j}+Z_{ij},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is mean-zero <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian. For <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;|\mu_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;|\mu_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>, reverse triangle inequality gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|X_{ij}|\geq|\mu_{j}|-|Z_{ij}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|X_{ij}|\geq|\mu_{j}|-|Z_{ij}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t\}\subseteq\{|X_{ij}|&gt;t\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t\}\subseteq\{|X_{ij}|&gt;t\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Using the sub-Gaussian tail bound</p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|\geq u)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-\frac{u^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|\geq u)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-\frac{u^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=|\mu_{j}|-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=|\mu_{j}|-t</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq 1-2\exp\!\left(-\frac{(|\mu_{j}|-t)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq 1-2\exp\!\left(-\frac{(|\mu_{j}|-t)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">This proves Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Elementwise Extreme Dominance). ‣ High-Dimensional Extreme-Value Amplification. ‣ 4 Mean Bias as the Dominant Source of Activation Outliers ‣ The Curse and Blessing of Mean Bias in FP4-Quantized LLM Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Dense Extreme Amplification by Mean Bias). ‣ High-Dimensional Extreme-Value Amplification. ‣ 4 Mean Bias as the Dominant Source of Activation Outliers ‣ The Curse and Blessing of Mean Bias in FP4-Quantized LLM Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{ij}=\mu_{j}+Z_{ij}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{ij}=\mu_{j}+Z_{ij},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent mean-zero sub-Gaussian random variables with variance proxy <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define the exceedance indicator</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{i}=\mathbf{1}\{|X_{ij}|&gt;t\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}=\mathbf{1}\{|X_{ij}|&gt;t\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and the total exceedance count</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{j}(t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}B_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{j}(t)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}B_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Mean-dominated regime</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mu_{j}|&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mu_{j}|&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By the reverse triangle inequality</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|X_{ij}|=|\mu_{j}+Z_{ij}|\geq|\mu_{j}|-|Z_{ij}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|X_{ij}|=|\mu_{j}+Z_{ij}|\geq|\mu_{j}|-|Z_{ij}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus if</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">then necessarily</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|X_{ij}|&gt;t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|X_{ij}|&gt;t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&lt;|\mu_{j}|-t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> is sub-Gaussian,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|\geq u)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-\frac{u^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|\geq u)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-\frac{u^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=|\mu_{j}|-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=|\mu_{j}|-t</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq 1-2\exp\!\left(-\frac{(|\mu_{j}|-t)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)\geq 1-2\exp\!\left(-\frac{(|\mu_{j}|-t)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Since the indicators <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent,</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{j}(t)]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}[B_{i}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{j}(t)]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{E}[B_{i}]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Using the lower bound above yields</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{j}(t)]\geq N\left(1-2\exp\!\left(-\frac{(|\mu_{j}|-t)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{j}(t)]\geq N\left(1-2\exp\!\left(-\frac{(|\mu_{j}|-t)^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Variance-only regime</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{ij}=Z_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{ij}=Z_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)=\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&gt;t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|X_{ij}|&gt;t)=\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&gt;t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the sub-Gaussian tail bound</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&gt;t)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&gt;t)\leq 2\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">we obtain</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[C_{j}(t)]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&gt;t)\leq 2N\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[C_{j}(t)]=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\mathbb{P}(|Z_{ij}|&gt;t)\leq 2N\exp\!\left(-\frac{t^{2}}{2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Interpretation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The two regimes differ fundamentally:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Mean-dominated: }C_{j}(t)=\Theta(N)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Mean-dominated: </mtext><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Mean-dominated: }C_{j}(t)=\Theta(N)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Variance-only: }C_{j}(t)=\mathcal{O}\!\left(Ne^{-t^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Variance-only: </mtext><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.654em;" width="0.654em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Variance-only: }C_{j}(t)=\mathcal{O}\!\left(Ne^{-t^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus a coherent mean shift produces a dense population of extreme activations across tokens, whereas purely variance-driven extremes are exponentially rare.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This scaling difference explains why mean bias becomes the dominant driver of activation outliers in large models.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
